' Deep-override fixture — THE MIDDLE, the object that gets cached.
'
' The override below is the point of the whole fixture. When this object is
' served from the cache, its child is never revisited: the OBJ block declaring
' `LSEED = 77` is not re-parsed, because parsing it is exactly what the hit
' skipped. So the override has to ride in the cache entry's instance sidecar or
' a warm build prints an empty Overrides column where a cold build prints a
' value — a warm/cold divergence, which the byte-equivalence harness compares
' maps precisely to catch.
OBJ
  kid : "ovr_deep_leaf" | LSEED = 77

PUB val() : result
  result := kid.val()
